WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.399 --> 00:00:03.399
Hello.

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:06.009
My name is John Bines and I’m a writer.

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:10.990
I thought about doing this video for awhile
but had held off because I’ve been actually

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.099
in the middle of transitioning.

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:18.750
I recently moved out to Los Angeles to further
my career as a writer and I’d like to take

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.259
a moment to tell you a little about myself.

00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:27.089
I’ve been in film and television now for
over 20 years.

00:00:27.089 --> 00:00:34.180
I started out after engaging in a lucrative
career in computer technologies and decided

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:40.790
that I really wanted to pursue my lifelong
goal to becoming a television and film writer.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:47.160
I quit my job and started working as a PA
(production assistant) on various music videos

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.300
and other projects.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:53.150
I eventually worked my way up over a number
of years to becoming an editor working for

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:59.460
people like Tom Fontana and Barry Levinson
and Dave Chappelle and many others.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:05.250
After awhile I realized that my career was
kind of stalemating as an editor and I started

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.310
to question what I was doing.

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:13.260
You know, like a shark at the bottom of the
ocean (I always like to use this as a parable)…like

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.250
a shark at the bottom of the ocean, in this
business you have to constantly keep moving.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.250
If you don’t, you literally will die.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:29.750
After awhile of editing for a number of people
for great, amazing projects, I decided to

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.550
seriously start writing.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:36.110
I started to write spec scripts for shows
that I had worked on.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:46.320
And writing original ideas of my own in the
form of screenplays and even started a novel.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:55.090
But I quickly found that as challenging as
it was reaching the goal to become an editor,

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:59.310
my desire to become a writer was even more
challenging.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:09.330
I had become very ill with a terminal illness
and very shortly after my faithful companion

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:15.079
dog (Fubu) of eleven years at the time had
been mauled by a pit bull.

00:02:15.079 --> 00:02:23.099
And in the mauling, I broke my hand actually
while the dog was mauling my dog trying to

00:02:23.099 --> 00:02:24.950
get him off of him.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:34.370
And my dog has since healed up and he’s
an amazing testament to courage, which is

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:39.019
one of the reasons why I wanted to actually
make this video was about courage and sometimes

00:02:39.019 --> 00:02:41.609
the courage it takes to continually pursue
your goals.

00:02:41.609 --> 00:02:48.120
Particularly if you want to become a writer
or stay even in the industry of film and television.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:56.610
So I’m there at my house with a broken hand
and healing a mauled dog and still dealing

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.220
with the terminal illness.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.730
I still had friends I was helping.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:04.819
I’ve always been a very generous person
and some friends were living with me and others

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:07.190
I was actually taking care of financially.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:13.620
And I started to ask myself, like at what
point is too much?

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.469
Is enough, enough?

00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:18.909
Where you keep giving of yourself and you’re
constantly having to take care of your own

00:03:18.909 --> 00:03:20.989
self and others.

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:26.610
And I started to think, what if you put that
burden on a 12-year-old boy?

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:31.290
Well, that actually created a television pilot
that I wrote called THE HEALER.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:36.680
It’s about a 12-year-old immigrant boy who
was gifted…or you could say cursed…with

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.250
the ability to heal.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:48.389
He teams up with a renegade, rogue CIA ex-AA
operative who is trained to kill (female operative)

00:03:48.389 --> 00:03:52.670
and they actually go on an adventure to save
the world.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:04:02.319
It’s a parable loosely based on the narrative
of Jesus Christ but more importantly reflective

00:04:02.319 --> 00:04:04.260
of what I felt I was going through in my own
life.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:10.659
One of the things I like to do is I write
about things that speak to me, things that

00:04:10.659 --> 00:04:12.540
are personal to me.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:18.019
And through all of my experiences in this
business and continually working I’ve always

00:04:18.019 --> 00:04:24.060
found that no matter how far I think I’ve
gone, I have so much farther to go and sometimes

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.169
I think I’m starting all over again.

00:04:26.169 --> 00:04:33.360
Which I have, I’ve recently moved to the
Los Angeles area to pursue a career in television

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:36.039
and hopefully to meet other writers and producers.

00:04:36.039 --> 00:04:43.699
I got an opportunity to direct a short film
and that was amazing and really trying to

00:04:43.699 --> 00:04:50.580
push to pursue this career that I’ve set
out upon over 20 years ago.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:58.020
So again my call of action is hopefully to
entice other producers to contact me or reach

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:01.680
out to me or reach out to me that I can build
relationships with to learn from and hopefully

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:09.360
to use my skills to help them and hopefully
get some information as to how I can further

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:16.830
my career as to how I can possibly work with
various people on different projects.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:25.360
One of the things I make a part of my day
(my daily regime) is watching videos from

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.840
Film Courage.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:35.530
All of the information (the amazing information),
the experiences of other writers really serve

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:44.820
to bolster my own sometimes lofty goals (I
call them) and also to let people know that

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:49.360
sometimes this road is not a fast one (it
takes awhile).

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:54.319
But my commitment, people ask me all of the
time “Why are you still doing this?”

00:05:54.319 --> 00:06:03.250
You know to me writing and creating dialogue
is intrinsic to me as the color of my skin

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.780
or my being a male for that matter.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:13.120
Again, this is to encourage others to hopefully
stay on your path and also another way of

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:20.389
my reaching out and hopefully expanding on
my contacts and people that can hopefully

00:06:20.389 --> 00:06:23.470
help me further my goals.

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:29.289
I just want to say thank you all and have
a good day and may we all reach our goals

00:06:29.289 --> 00:06:34.940
no matter how lofty they seem to be and just
stay on your path and stick to what you’re

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:38.439
doing and eventually things will work out.

00:06:38.439 --> 00:06:39.439
Thank you!

00:06:39.439 --> 00:06:39.446
Contact John Bines to read THE HEALER

